t(1, 400, """Do not say “Yusif” but say “Yusuf” - do not say “Yunis” but say “Yunus”""")

t(1, 700, """“Have those who believe not yet realized that had Allah willed, He would have guided all people?”""")

t(1, 1010, """How many people make light of an evil word, and make light of hurling accusations, and split open chests at a prompting from Satan, who deludes them that they are speaking truth and rightness. For to what wicked soul has Allah the Exalted disclosed the hidden secret of another, that it should say of so-and-so such-and-such evil and accuse him of what he is innocent of, while its owner's tongue, in uttering abuse, is untied, let loose, racing the wind in audacity and injustice. So, beautiful patience""")

t(1, 1385, """“And why should we not rely upon Allah when He has guided us to our ways? We will surely be patient with the harm you do us. And upon Allah let those who rely, rely.”

“We certainly know that your chest is constricted by what they say (97). So glorify the praise of your Lord and be among those who prostrate (98). And worship your Lord until the certainty comes to you.”""")

t(1, 1905, """The ladder carried sideways: true, it bumps into people; true, it harms them for a period of time; true, it wounds them and makes their blood flow. But in the end it breaks, is smashed, and stops hurting people. A moment must come ..""")

t(2, 1090, """When people said: “A big problem will occur in the world,” I said: Let us move on to what comes after the problem! For the problem has its people, and what comes after the problem has its people! And this is the ABC of the science of crisis management! One of the most important branches of the Western management sciences.

Nations rise only through unpacking the mind! And the mind can only be unpacked by a thinking whose basis is the mind's speed of response to the next step, not only to what has happened and to the reality dominating the psychological state! Nations rise by planning! Nations rise by a will supported from heaven! Nations rise by understanding the truths of life correctly, and the proof of it is wisdom of mind, composure of soul and soundness of logic! Nations rise by grasping what is hidden from people's understanding and their minds! Nations rise by trust in Allah the Almighty, our Lord, because He is the owner of everything! Everything is subject to Him, hallowed be His names, with the submission of the subdued, not the submission of one who chooses; even if the submissive one surrenders willingly, he is under subjugation from beginning to end! And nations rise when there are born in their lands, in their villages, in their cities, in their valleys and in their mountains young men and young women .. men and women .. who believe that with Allah they can .. and believe that with Allah they are able .. and believe that with Allah they will cross over!""")

t(3, 555, """My gift to you tonight .. on condition that you do not suffer from back problems .. Are you looking for real youth? Move about inside your home while carrying weights .. going to the balcony .. going to the kitchen .. moving between the living room and the bedroom .. Then make that a daily habit .. not once a week .. and you will begin to notice the real difference, if Allah the Exalted wills""")

t(3, 2110, """The speeches of Maduro, and before him Netanyahu and his team, and throughout history many before them .. Agitation .. anger .. shouting! Speeches that do not befit leaders who own strong states .. Political discourse to the nation is not a Friday sermon .. and political discourse to the nation is not a speech inside parliament .. Strong words are enough to inflame the feelings of the masses without shouting! Strong words are enough to be heard by the masses like bullets exploding without shouting .. A sharp tone is enough .. the strength of the voice is enough while the speaker speaks, and the vigor of the voice is enough, not its loudness; the vigor of the voice is one thing and its loudness quite another .. Shouting is a clear substitute for the strength of the vocabulary and for all the qualities I listed in the previous line! The leaders of the United States, Russia and China never shout when they address the masses .. Maduro ruled a completely collapsed state for years .. Maduro's agitated discourse recalls the outbursts of Abdel Nasser, Yasser Arafat and others! In modern international politics the West established an oratorical custom for showing strength! The strength of emotional steadiness; it presented it as proof of the strength of the state, and practised it. But its speeches are leftist, shaky and weak, addressing masses who do not see that there is any challenge facing them at all. For what challenge do the English, the Danes, the Germans, the French, the Italians or the Spaniards feel? Nothing! So 80 years are the age of European prosperity""")

t(4, 205, """and of calm political speeches that bring on sleep! Today Trump uses strong words when he speaks to his nation .. Putin and Xi also use strong words .. But there is no spirit in any of the three! Not Trump, not Xi, not Putin. The reason is that they carry the message of this world, and the message of this world does not make the voice strong even if its owner does not shout! The message of this world is always hollow from within; it makes the discourse hollow however strong its words are, it makes it hollow from within, empty. For the three of them are not fighting for the interests of mankind, the salvation of mankind and the happiness of mankind; otherwise the matter would be different! The three of them are fighting for the interests of their countries, and their countries are not all mankind!

As for those who fight for the sake of mankind, if they whisper they ignite enthusiasm, and if they appear even without speaking they inflame feelings, and if they begin to speak the whole world roars before they have even begun their talk. Because the strength of those who carry the concern of mankind is not from themselves! It is something that is neither sold nor bought! Something that Trump, Xi and Putin cannot buy! They can never buy it!""")

t(4, 1040, """The “Maduro” operation may turn into a precedent in international politics .. Taiwan China .. Zelensky Putin .. ((may)) turn into an international method of showing off strength!""")

t(4, 1385, """After the world war, oil will not have a global strategic value like its value today, because of the destruction of millions of factories. And making oil strategic once again, and influential in international relations and in the world economy, will require the emergence of a consuming, non-manufacturing nation, because mankind does not have a long time to build up an industrial accumulation from zero and to train generations upon generations! All of that is over.

The equation for a nation's success in imposing its vision in international relations will continue to require its dominance over all the sources of energy in the world, even Russia and Venezuela, fundamentally; for even these two regions could offer the alternative to the world's factories, and then the oil of the Arabs would have no value!

But if the Arabs want dominance over the movement of the world economy, they cannot achieve this dominance without their dominance over the sources of oil in the world and their complete control of the tap! Otherwise, with many oil taps existing, you cannot impose your word in international relations.""")

t(4, 2255, """My little ones: do not go too far from home, so that my heart does not ache!""")

t(5, 1215, """When, in the future, by the permission of Allah the Exalted, the resources of the Muslims are enough to build a clinic inside every residential neighborhood, why should people have to stand in queues inside hospitals?""")

t(6, 240, """On understanding the hadith: “The Arabs on that day are few” .. a prophetic statement that the pure Arabs will reach the end of time being few. This is the case today, even before the Dajjal, but not in the sense of the annihilation that may possibly occur (partially) before the Dajjal.

As for the question of Umm Sharik, may Allah be pleased with her, about the Arabs: did the reader of the hadith think she was asking about the Copts of Egypt? About the Amazigh of North Africa? About the Romans of the Levant and the non-Arabs of Iraq? They were only tribes, not the great majority. And even if there were millions of Arabs in Iraq and the Levant, which is an incorrect assumption, they are today fewer than a single Islamic country; so how many were they in Iraq and the Levant 1447 years ago, if this is their state today? Even at the time of the question of Umm Sharik, may Allah be pleased with her, they were few amid the non-Arabs and the Romans! And we are speaking of the time of nomadism; Umm Sharik need not have known of Arabs living there in the heart of Iraq and the Levant so as to mean them by her question. The homeland of the pure-blooded Arabs was the Arabian Peninsula.

As for the hadith, as I said in an earlier post, it is a miracle among the signs of prophethood that the Arabs reach the end of time in this fewness. The reason is that the Arabian Peninsula, until the fall of the Ottoman state, was tribes or scattered settlements until a recent era (100 years), except the Hijaz as a center; the services of the Ottoman state clearly reached only the Hijaz. Whoever reads the books of modern history in the Arabian Peninsula (the place of the few Arabs) will find that famines used to strike the Arabian Peninsula and wipe out half the tribe, or a quarter of it! So the Arabs are in fact few today. As for the saying of the Prophet ﷺ to Umm Sharik when she asked about the Dajjal, his saying to her: “The Arabs on that day are few”, it does not necessarily mean that before the Dajjal they were many! For it is conceivable that the Prophet ﷺ would not burden his speech by saying to Umm Sharik, for example: “They are few before the Dajjal and few in his time.” This, in my view, is a sound consideration: the Prophet not burdening or expanding his speech, because the noble prophetic address and the prophetic statement have always proceeded on brevity and answering without expansion.""")

t(6, 1470, """O speakers .. O noble ones: have mercy on people. A state of lack of concentration dominates many of the speakers, and I do not know, is it sorcery? Do not say “soon the Arabs will be few”, for the hadith “the Arabs are few” is about the day the Dajjal appears. But some of our brothers the speakers do not concentrate while they talk to people; they talk about the time of the Ummah's glory and say “the Arabs on that day are few!” A very, very high state of confusion among them! It has only one explanation! Sorcery or weak memory!
The hadith: “People will flee from the Dajjal until they reach the mountains.” Umm Sharik said: “O Messenger of Allah, where are the Arabs on that day?” He said: “They are few.” This is a well-known hadith. Many people know it by heart! The hadith says (the Dajjal). Where are we and where is the Dajjal?

My comment: “few” does not mean annihilation! If all the hundreds of millions of this Ummah were brought from Indonesia, Pakistan and Bangladesh, and a billion non-Arab Muslims were gathered into the geography of the Middle East, the Arabs among them would be few. This is also the meaning of the time of the Dajjal. There is no might and no power except with Allah. The hadith is about the time of the Dajjal, and our brothers the speakers tell people it is the time of the Mahdi! Allah is the One whose help is sought. As for “few” by which annihilation is meant, there is no denying this, because the sign of the Smoke will leave no one, and Allah knows best, and not the Arabs alone.

Reflecting on the hadiths and gathering all of them into a single, deficient, incomplete understanding never reveals the complete picture. Where is the hadith “The Hour will come while the Romans are the most numerous of people”? Today the Chinese and the Indians are the most numerous of people (by race), so where will they go? If the Prophet ﷺ did not mention the annihilation of the Chinese and the Indians, then this hadith mentions their annihilation clearly! For when the Prophet ﷺ says, in meaning not in wording: “Many nations will perish and the Romans will be the most numerous of people”, he is speaking here of a clear meaning of annihilation. As for the Arabs, their fewness is not necessarily due to annihilation. What is the number of the Arabs today? The Arabs are not the people of the conquered lands, Egypt, North Africa, all of Iraq and all of the Levant. Rather, tribes of the Arabs lived in those regions, but the root of the stock is not Arab. The Arabs in the prophetic wording are not North Africa, the Levant and Iraq, but the people of the Arabian Peninsula and the Arab tribes that lived in the Levantine desert adjoining the north of the Arabian Peninsula. And how many are the people of the Arabian Peninsula today? 35 million? What is their numerical value amid a billion and a half Muslims? Their numerical value is nothing.

I ask that we all be disciplined and not take the authentic hadiths about the Dajjal and his time and place them in a time before his time, for this""")

t(7, 215, """is something that makes people not understand matters correctly.""")

t(7, 555, """Do not claim of Islam that it is a religion of shacks and ruins; shacks and ruins are the culture of your own head! Islam is more entitled than any creed or (religion) on this earth to offer its society the cleanest homes, the most beautiful services, the finest institutions and the greatest cities in infrastructure! Those who do not know that, what can we do for them if they do not comprehend?! If they do not know?! If they do not understand?! By Allah, the last of our concerns is that they comprehend, the last of our concerns is that they know, and the last of our concerns is that they understand! Every person represents his own experience! The one who has traveled around the world and seen what is in it represents a broad, wide experience of understanding and perception, and the one who has lived his whole life inside a shack thinks the world must be a shack, or else the Lord has been disobeyed and the Lord has been angered! These are your own delusions! You manufactured delusions for yourself and lived in them! Our religion and our Islam have nothing to do with these delusions.

How I pity these people!""")

t(7, 1335, """After a 100-year journey of exhausting the Muslim human being! Of killing his spirit (figuratively). Of shattering his morale, crushing all his will and darkening the world in his eyes .. After 100 years of standing in queues .. waiting for paperwork as though it were an entry card to the Paradise of the Most Merciful! Riding 5 public transports to reach a government office! The bad treatment in poor countries! Enacting laws that make completing a government transaction a far-fetched wish!""")

t(8, 405, """In foreseeing the future with understanding and awareness: teaching the Arabic language to a section of the employees of government departments, since the Western mentality is quicker to respond in putting into effect the culture of respecting the human being and dealing with him with courtesy and respect, compared with others (without generalizing)""")

t(8, 1935, """The elderly with chronic illnesses and the ordeal of going to hospitals for tests! If he is in fact called elderly .. and called a patient .. how is he required to bear the hardship of going to a hospital and waiting in queues?! In my own experience, when I was ill years ago, I felt how disastrous it was to move from one place to another in the neighborhood I live in, while the body was full of weakness, fatigue and exhaustion .. Even a distance of two meters of walking was like a slow death .. The matter was a real torment .. These worn-out, tired elderly bodies are truly tormented by going to hospitals for tests. The sick elderly are among the weakest of the weak in society .. They are weaker than women and children .. By them societies are tested, and unfortunately the failure rates are very high, whereas an ambulance passing by the sick elderly person spares him all the hardship.""")

t(9, 1245, """The future is a promise .. and when the promise is from our Almighty Lord it is surely coming .. And the most beautiful journey in the history of the Ummah, after the beauty of the first, which was with the Prophet ﷺ, has not begun yet .. So whoever has grasped the promise and what is in it, let him shelter himself on the mountain of protection from tribulations as much as he can, let him send ahead before Allah that by which evil ends are averted, and let him show Allah the Exalted sincerity from himself; perhaps Allah the Exalted will grant him an abundant share of the journey""")

t(10, 355, """Why should you have to leave your residential neighborhood to complete your government paperwork - passport - identity card - birth certificate - ownership of land and house?""")

t(10, 1830, """This hadith is weak and its attribution to the Prophet ﷺ is not sound: (After the Mahdi there will be the Qahtani, and by the One who sent me with the truth, he is not inferior to him). It has spread among many people.

When I was asked about the Qahtani, I said: it is authentically established in al-Bukhari and Muslim that there is a man from Qahtan who will rule the people at the end of time and be severe with them. There are no authentic hadiths that specify whether his emergence is in the time of the Mahdi, after his death immediately, or some time after his death, in the time of the prophet of Allah Isa. If someone says that for him it is certain that it will be in the time of the prophet of Allah Isa, I say: his severity toward the people does not hold up, for two reasons:
First: the presence of the prophet of Allah Isa, peace be upon him, among the people, and the prophets are a mercy on earth.
Second: the small number of people and the departure of the tribulations of the world from them, so over what would he be severe?

Even so, the two reasons I have put forward cannot be decisive, for they are not of the strength by which a proof stands. Some have held that the Qahtani is the very person of the Imam, and this is a claim with no proof. The Imam has been described, in what Ahmad narrated with a good chain, as one with whom the dweller of heaven and the dweller of earth are pleased, and people's contentment does not combine with severity toward them, for being severe with people frightens them, and that is not of the prophetic method by which the years of the Imam's rule were described. The Prophet ﷺ was not severe with people nor did he drive them with his staff. Accordingly the Qahtani is a separate figure.""")

t(11, 190, """when its time and timing are .. Allah alone knows, since there is no text specifying whether his emergence is at the beginning of the time of the prophet of Allah Isa, peace be upon him, or in the middle of the time of the prophet of Allah Isa, peace be upon him, or after the time of the prophet of Allah Isa, peace be upon him. So whoever has a hadith, authentic or with a good chain, about the time of his appearance may put it in the comments, because some researchers raise this question in private about the time of his appearance.""")

t(11, 665, """Speaking about religion without specialization is a crime! Speaking about religion has two sides, with no third. Subtleties in the deep meanings behind the verses; this is open to all if it agrees with the basis of the interpretation of the Book of Allah the Exalted, and it needs no specialization. For example: a person reflects on one of the punishments of the people of the Fire as they scream and cry out, and says: perhaps, and Allah knows best, one of the reasons for their screaming is that they caused the screaming of Allah's servants in this world. This does not conflict with the Book of Allah, and there is no alteration in it of the text that speaks of the screaming of the people of the Fire. This needs no specialization. But for a person to come and play with the words of the Book of Allah, to bring what the predecessors did not bring in understanding the plain, clear meanings, to alter, to say that the Qur'an has an outward and an inward, and to speak about the meanings of the Book from his own mind while he holds no linguistic or jurisprudential academic degree that would make him competent and firmly grounded in understanding the language on which the words of the Qur'an are based, this is not an effort to reflect on the Qur'anic subtleties, which is permitted to any educated Muslim as long as it accords with the rule I mentioned. Rather, this is innovation in the Book of Allah by an ignorant, pretentious person who thinks himself a scholar. This is a general statement, because this disease - the disease of self-admiration upon ignorance - has spread, become general and overwhelming, and the affliction from it has grown great. Many have dared against the Book of Allah the Exalted and gone on issuing fatwas about it, saying: Allah taught us, Allah showed us, Allah made us understand! What knowledge did our Lord teach you? The reflection by which you fabricate against the Book of Allah is a reflection that needs scholars, not every Tom, Dick and Harry who read a verse, and Allah the Exalted opened something to him, so he said: I will explain the Book of Allah to you! This is frivolity, and it is among the grave matters that bring down the punishment of Allah the Exalted. Whoever holds the Book of Allah the Exalted this cheap has none to blame but himself.""")

t(11, 1665, """Do you have a permit from the government to speak about religion? Where is your permit?""")

t(12, 575, """A scientific study, one year old, reveals that a crime against humanity took place in the seventies of the twentieth century .. The study says that one of the most important causes of the immune diseases that have struck people terrifyingly since the seventies, and swelled to hit hundreds of millions of people, was mistaken medical advice to people to stay away from full-fat milk, and deluding people that it is harmful to the arteries! The study also comes back to confirm what earlier studies reached about the benefits of animal fats. But everyone who suffers from diseases of the arteries and the heart today, I advise them to consult the doctor. Animal fats, together with body movement and exerting activity, are very beneficial for the healthy. As for patients who have been afflicted with inflammation of the arteries and are undergoing treatments, these are no longer healthy, so they must not take any new steps without consulting their doctors.""")

t(12, 1280, """The oldest hospital of modern medicine in the Arab world .. Qasr al-Ayni in Egypt .. Qasr = palace, because the building was originally built as a palace, and it was built in the year 1466 CE .. Al-Ayni refers to the builder of the palace, who was of Turkish origin, his origin going back to the city of (Ayn Tab): the Mamluk emir Shihab al-Din Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Ayni. He was nicknamed al-Ayni after the Turkish city (Ayn Tab), and he held the post of Emir of the Hajj. In the year 1827 Muhammad Ali took the palace as a hospital, when he moved the school of medicine to the palace, and it became the oldest school of medicine in the Arab world. Generations of Egyptians and Arabs have been treated in the Qasr al-Ayni hospital in Egypt. May Allah protect Egypt, and protect every land, village and city in the lands of Islam.""")

t(13, 845, """As many have warned about this moral crisis, whose age is now a full century .. Either he harasses or he describes to his colleagues! Until when, O some fathers and O some husbands? Real men excepted.""")

h(13, 1400, """… in the maternity ward the male doctors, by Allah most of them, if they do not harass, go out and describe to one another, to the point that I changed my department completely .. And after that, when I got married, by Allah I never went to a male doctor, all of them women doctors; even for childbirth I go private and stipulate that the whole staff be women, and even if I die, it is forbidden …""")

t(13, 2310, """The western Californian stands shoulder to shoulder beside his brother the eastern New Yorker, and together they defend one dream called the United States .. a dream they do not want to collapse ..

But here in our region, the owners of channels more trivial than triviality sharpen their tongues, at one time against the people of the East with Maghrebi tongues, and at another against the people of the Maghreb with Eastern tongues .. And these or those are surely promised, one day, what the people of Egypt call (and where it hurts you).""")

t(14, 415, """In the chest there is an idol! .. It is no longer around the Ka'bah .. no longer throughout the Arabian Peninsula .. It moved into the chest 1440 years ago .. It has become more dangerous than its visible form upon the earth!

((And they say: “Are we to leave our gods for a mad poet?”)) .. Our gods that are in our chests? Gods in the chest! Worshipped more intensely than the worship of al-Lat, al-Uzza, Manat and Hubal!
((Those who dispute about the signs of Allah without any authority having come to them, there is nothing in their chests but pride which they will never attain)) - and pride is the greatest idol on earth, absolutely!""")

t(15, 1105, """A little while ago someone came out and said that there is something called a polar vortex that has collapsed, and that this will mean the coming of great snowstorms that will cover Europe and the Arab region, and he added that the Little Ice Age will begin as of this year, to become usual in every winter in our Arab region .. For some time I have felt that ice is coming to our region in the coming years and that snow in winter will be a natural sight in our Arab lands .. It was merely a feeling that came out in the published pictures .. and it was a strong feeling that dominated the soul! So if that feeling is truly headed for our region .. then, as I said before .. we are, by the power of Allah the Exalted, heading toward major changes at the level of the environment, the growth of crops in the barren desert, the availability of water if Allah the Exalted wills, and the change of the form of life in our region for the better, if Allah the Exalted wills. The reason for this is not only the news about the snow, but also the falling of beneficial rain all year round, by Allah's permission, and not only in a month or two. That same beneficial rain will also increase the abundance of fresh water and the formation of lakes, and improve the levels of water wealth, which will allow, by the permission of Allah the Exalted, the raising of livestock and the farming of what secures food security for the region. These are neither simple nor ordinary matters. This is a comprehensive and complete transition of the region from a state of environmental weakness that has long affected it to a state of environmental strength that is very important in the making of the superpower.""")

t(16, 890, """We are commanded to verify before responding, and there is no accusation at all in this against the brother who conveyed it, but only giving the fairness of verification its due, nothing more.
Is this talk true? Did Abd al-Aziz al-Qahtani really speak about the Book of Allah the Exalted in this way?

One of the brothers commented in the questions corner and wrote:
Ustadh Faraj, have you followed the channel of the Yemeni sheikh Abdulaziz al-Qahtani and what he publishes in explaining the word “mathani”, with which Allah described His Book, the Noble Qur'an

Reply

@ma3faraj

I have not followed him

Reply

@Ramadanmobaraknew

@ma3faraj Al-Qahtani interpreted the word “mathani”, relying on the language and on the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (I was given the Qur'an and its like with it), as meaning the thing that has two sides; so every verse in the Qur'an has two meanings, a literal meaning and a figurative meaning. He showed the two meanings in many verses, and also showed that this rhetorical power in a single statement, that is, two meanings at once, is something no Arab could utter the like of, and that this is the miracle of the Qur'an before which the eloquent of Quraysh were powerless
Reply
@Ramadanmobaraknew

Look, for example, at the saying of Allah the Exalted (And proclaim the Hajj among the people; they will come to you on foot and on every lean camel, coming from every deep mountain pass). The literal meaning of His saying “rijalan” is those who walk on their feet, and its figurative meaning is the males. So did Allah mean the first or the second""")

t(17, 150, """In the questions corner one of the sisters asked a question about the will of the people of the Fire. I would like to add something I have not said before about the people of the Fire being tormented by being given (will). It is astonishing that the people of the Fire should have a will, but when we understand the reason, our astonishment will pass. It is a personal reasoning in understanding the verse; if I am right, it is from Allah the Almighty, our Lord, alone.

The verse is the saying of our Almighty Lord, hallowed be His names: (Whenever they want to get out of it, out of anguish, they are returned into it, and: Taste the punishment of the burning)

I had explained the matter of this verse in detail perhaps a month ago. I said that the will of the people of the Fire occurs but fails, because it is inside the Fire; like one who climbs a smooth, slippery wall trying to get out of the Fire and reaches the top of the wall, then is brought down into the Fire. His will was realized as a will, it has existence, but it failed as a will. Because the verse says “they are returned into it” and not “they are returned to it”. Had the verse said “they are returned to it”, that would indicate that the will of the people of the Fire succeeds and that they leave the confines of the Fire entirely and are then returned to those confines, and this is what the verse did not say. So the verse established that they have a will, but it is a failed will, and they are given it so that their regret grows; thus they go on living the failed will always and forever.

As for my reasoning about the matter of the will of the people of the Fire, and perhaps one of the reasons for granting it to them: one of the aspects of their being tormented with the failed will, as a reasoning from me, and Allah the Exalted is higher and knows best, is that in the abode of this world they used to torment Allah's creation by making their wills fail; they set laws on earth that left people besieged in their wills, so they found no solutions to their problems. Man had been given a will by Allah the Exalted in the abode of this world so that he might strive on earth, succeed and live in dignity, but the tyrants stripped it from him and made it worthless at the level of action, by imposing laws that kill his will. They robbed the weak on earth of will, and the weak one lived using his will and failing, then using it and failing, then using it and failing, and so on, time after time without end. He lived regret, lived grief, and lived distress in the abode of this world. So, and Allah knows best, the people of the Fire are tormented by being given the failed will as one of the kinds of torment for them, just as they tormented Allah's servants in the abode of this world by making their will a failed one that does not succeed, so that the oppressed lived this torment and suffered because of it.""")

t(17, 1675, """A number of the brothers were, until recently, still preoccupied with the issue of the sign of the Smoke. I have responded on this issue here more than once, and refuted the severe weakness and great feebleness in the statements of those who herald its occurrence soon. But since I was reminded of it today by the question of one of the brothers a little while ago in the questions corner, here is a sufficient, satisfying answer that I have not written before, about my objection to the argument that this sign is near, as has been much promoted, that it is imminent!

First: the claim that the earth has been filled with corruption, and so it is natural for Allah the Exalted to send a cosmic sign, and therefore the sign of the Smoke is imminent and coming, is an unsound claim according to the scientific method, its tools, ways and approaches. For mankind became corrupt in many stages of it, with what was greater than its corruption today. The Tatars left no land without corrupting it and slaughtering its people; because of them prayers were prevented, mosques were burned, millions of women were taken captive, not thousands, and innocent souls were killed in the millions, not in the thousands. Yet no heavenly sign came; what came was only the Tatars' destroying one another and weakness entering upon them, then the door was opened for the Muslims and they were able to defeat them.

The evidences in human history are many that there is no relation between the descent of a heavenly sign and the corruption of the people of the earth, except what was before Islam, then indeed yes: the drowning of Pharaoh, the destruction of the people of the prophet of Allah Nuh, the destruction of Ad, Thamud, the people of the prophet of Allah Lut, and others. Then those punishments passed and the message of the prophet of Allah Isa, peace be upon him, came; great states arose and great states fell, and no cosmic signs occurred, for plague and wars are not cosmic signs; rather, mutual repelling took place on earth, and the laws of mutual repelling, not laws of punishment. Then came a recorded, well-known cosmic sign in the time of Abraha the Abyssinian, and its reason is known and clear: the matter was in a village in a small, narrow valley, in which were a few hundred weak human beings and a newborn who was born to be a light for the earth ﷺ. So all the means of the laws of mutual repelling had fallen away, and at that moment all the ways out of resisting, repulsing and defending were absent, and there was no great state to back Quraysh, clash with Abraha and keep him from the Sacred House of Allah, so that the law of mutual repelling would be and take place. So the law of punishment occurred. But are we today nations on""")

t(18, 205, """earth resembling the valley of Bakkah and its weak, oppressed people before a massive army? The answer is 100% no, because there is a legislation called Islam, and a vast, far-flung Ummah required to follow the legislation in fighting and in defense. We are not in the valley of Bakkah with Abraha about to enter its roads. Even in the defense of individuals today, the law of punishment is possible, but we see that the law of mutual repelling is what is taking place: Allah sends one party against another and they clash. So one should not confuse what was before Islam with what came after it as regards the laws, nor confuse with the necessities of the law of punishment that has not ended, such as the punishment of Gog and Magog, which is of the laws of punishment, not of the laws of mutual repelling.

The Ummah has a legislation, and it is required to show Allah the Exalted from itself what the legislation has made obligatory upon it. And the claim that the sign of the Smoke is the only thing that can empower the Muslims to rise is also a claim whose scientific reasoning is weak, because the evidences of the Ummah's history contradict this claim clearly and without ambiguity. There is a huge and great difference of laws in the life of mankind before Islam and after it, and failing to grasp this issue is a problem in understanding the present and the future, and causes any researcher to fall into errors of foresight that are not small. Also, those who say that the sign of the Smoke is about to occur and that it is before the Mahdi were asked a question more than once here on the channel, a year or two ago, to prove that the sign of the Smoke will not wipe out electricity, and no one answered!

Events greater than the war on the Strip have befallen the Ummah, and Allah the Exalted sent down His help upon the Ummah without a major sign. The sign of the Smoke is a sign that heralds the end of civilization, and it contradicts 100% all the hadiths with authentic chains that came about the time of the Mahdi, and collides completely with those hadiths. Its promoters have long indicated that it is near and imminent and will take us by surprise at any moment, until people thought from this description of time that it would happen very soon. The words of the researchers who held this (view) were clear more than once that it appears before the Imam Mahdi, and this, as I said, is a reasoning that blows up the hadiths of the Mahdi utterly and takes him out of his unseen context with its clear details of which the Prophet ﷺ informed!

And Allah is the One whose help is sought""")

t(18, 1640, """A post dedicated to placing questions""")

t(18, 1935, """Welcome .. Today we will reveal the truth to you .. the truth that the world media hid from you for long years .. Today we will introduce you to Islam! What is it? How did it begin? Why do we believe in it? What is its stance toward the other nations? How was it wronged by Muslims, some of whom were ignorant while others were traitors to Islam who deliberately distorted it? Today you will learn everything.""")
